WEBVTT

00:01:41.080 --> 00:01:43.290
<b>Odd Jobs Gin-chan</b>

00:01:41.540 --> 00:01:43.290
What? A tour?

00:01:43.640 --> 00:01:45.240
My friend, Satsuki-chan,

00:01:45.270 --> 00:01:46.930
asked for an educational tour of

00:01:46.930 --> 00:01:48.550
Odd Jobs to fulfill an assignment.

00:01:49.010 --> 00:01:52.180
Stop offering to do stuff 
that's a pain in the ass.

00:01:52.180 --> 00:01:54.460
If she wants to see us at work,

00:01:54.460 --> 00:01:56.010
we don't have any jobs today.

00:01:56.010 --> 00:01:57.810
We haven't had any jobs in forever.

00:01:58.400 --> 00:02:00.090
We don't want to ruin

00:02:00.090 --> 00:02:03.310
the hopes and dreams of young children.

00:02:03.530 --> 00:02:04.540
No!

00:02:04.540 --> 00:02:06.920
I want to show them how great 
Odd Jobs Kagura-chan is!

00:02:06.920 --> 00:02:08.570
Do something about it, scumbags!

00:02:08.570 --> 00:02:10.690
Stop tacking on random insults.

00:02:11.350 --> 00:02:12.320
She's here!

00:02:12.720 --> 00:02:15.270
You guys better act like grown-ups.

00:02:15.270 --> 00:02:17.450
Don't do anything weird!

00:02:18.080 --> 00:02:19.450
Welcome, Satsuki-chan!

00:02:19.870 --> 00:02:21.570
Sorry, Kagura-chan.

00:02:21.570 --> 00:02:22.830
I'm sure that you're busy.

00:02:23.210 --> 00:02:25.390
Thank you!

00:02:25.830 --> 00:02:28.840
<b>I Can't Remember a Damn 
Thing About the Factory Tour</b>

00:02:30.130 --> 00:02:31.760
This is our strategist/Supreme

00:02:31.760 --> 00:02:34.310
Commander of Eastern Operations, 
Strategos Shimura.

00:02:34.310 --> 00:02:35.590
Supreme Commander of 
Eastern Operations?!

00:02:35.970 --> 00:02:38.430
Shut up and follow my lead.

00:02:38.430 --> 00:02:40.740
Just say stuff that sounds cool.

00:02:40.740 --> 00:02:43.770
Wow, Supreme Commander 
of Eastern Operations...

00:02:43.770 --> 00:02:47.100
Um, what kind of work 
do you do at Odd Jobs?

00:02:47.100 --> 00:02:49.580
O-Our president will explain that,

00:02:49.580 --> 00:02:50.610
so come on inside.

00:02:51.780 --> 00:02:55.290
President, the kids are 
here for their tour.

00:02:55.290 --> 00:02:57.030
May we come in?

00:03:03.920 --> 00:03:06.630
He's turned the room into 
a workshop or something...

00:03:07.500 --> 00:03:08.710
Uh, President?

00:03:08.710 --> 00:03:10.050
Bah, it's no use.

00:03:10.050 --> 00:03:13.010
The naked refuses to 
jack in to the solid.

00:03:13.070 --> 00:03:14.800
U-Uh, President...

00:03:14.800 --> 00:03:16.450
Could you shut the door?

00:03:16.450 --> 00:03:17.500
If you let the heat escape,

00:03:17.500 --> 00:03:19.390
my Patriot will cool down and harden.

00:03:19.390 --> 00:03:21.550
Oh, s-sorry!

00:03:21.550 --> 00:03:23.200
What's a Patriot supposed to be?

00:03:23.200 --> 00:03:23.950
I have no idea what's going on,

00:03:23.950 --> 00:03:25.390
but the president sounds 
like a real craftsman.

00:03:25.390 --> 00:03:28.770
Um, we're here to see you at work.

00:03:28.770 --> 00:03:31.210
Do you prefer Calcutta or Meso Gear?

00:03:31.210 --> 00:03:31.730
Huh?

00:03:32.050 --> 00:03:36.110
If you're here, you must prefer one.

00:03:36.630 --> 00:03:37.700
Ignore them.

00:03:37.700 --> 00:03:39.120
Ignore their pleas for help.

00:03:40.190 --> 00:03:42.170
I-I like Calcutta.

00:03:42.170 --> 00:03:43.260
M-Me too.

00:03:43.260 --> 00:03:44.010
They randomly chose one!

00:03:44.010 --> 00:03:44.750
Me too.

00:03:44.040 --> 00:03:45.620
They randomly chose Calcutta!

00:03:46.040 --> 00:03:48.050
I see, you choose Calcutta.

00:03:48.050 --> 00:03:50.130
Hmph, how precocious of you.

00:03:50.690 --> 00:03:51.330
Here.

00:03:51.330 --> 00:03:52.880
Calcutta should be 
enjoyed while it's hot.

00:03:53.140 --> 00:03:55.020
Th-Thank you very much!

00:03:55.020 --> 00:03:56.260
This is Calcutta?

00:03:56.260 --> 00:03:57.450
It looks like coffee.

00:03:57.450 --> 00:03:59.820
Why didn't you just ask them 
if they liked coffee or not?!

00:03:59.820 --> 00:04:01.310
You're pissing me off!

00:04:01.540 --> 00:04:05.250
I once tried to be 
brave and try Calcutta.

00:04:05.250 --> 00:04:07.420
But now I'm a devout fan of Meso Gear.

00:04:06.080 --> 00:04:15.050
<b>Edo Strawberry Milk</b>

00:04:07.420 --> 00:04:09.490
I believe that my 
dedication to Meso Gear

00:04:09.490 --> 00:04:11.910
was a product of that bitter experience.

00:04:12.020 --> 00:04:13.820
He's throwing together 
a bunch of fancy phrases

00:04:13.820 --> 00:04:15.070
to say absolutely nothing at all!

00:04:15.070 --> 00:04:16.950
Can we get started?

00:04:16.950 --> 00:04:19.950
What do you Odd Jobs people even do?

00:04:20.170 --> 00:04:23.130
Well, it's quite difficult 
to explain what we do.

00:04:23.130 --> 00:04:25.580
You could say that we are 
essentially a secret society

00:04:25.580 --> 00:04:28.470
involved in the production 
and sale of this Patriot.

00:04:28.470 --> 00:04:30.670
That would make us Patriot salesmen!

00:04:30.930 --> 00:04:32.010
What is this Pastry...

00:04:32.010 --> 00:04:32.830
Patriot.

00:04:32.830 --> 00:04:35.670
What is this Patriot used for?

00:04:37.210 --> 00:04:40.480
Don't make me laugh.

00:04:40.480 --> 00:04:43.380
What is a Patriot used for, Kagura-kun?

00:04:43.380 --> 00:04:47.600
Kids say the darndest 
things, right, President?

00:04:47.600 --> 00:04:48.330
What's with them?

00:04:48.330 --> 00:04:49.190
They're pissing me off!

00:04:49.590 --> 00:04:51.690
Let me ask you this then.

00:04:51.690 --> 00:04:54.940
What's that below your nose?

00:04:54.940 --> 00:04:57.280
Every person has a peculiar indentation

00:04:57.280 --> 00:04:58.880
between their nose and mouth.

00:04:58.880 --> 00:05:00.950
What is that used for?

00:05:01.280 --> 00:05:03.160
I-I don't know...

00:05:03.160 --> 00:05:04.430
Of course.

00:05:04.430 --> 00:05:06.250
Now, back to the Patriot.

00:05:07.120 --> 00:05:08.540
It's pretty much like that.

00:05:08.540 --> 00:05:09.870
So you don't know either?!

00:05:10.370 --> 00:05:12.110
Whether it's the indentation 
below your nose

00:05:12.110 --> 00:05:14.400
or the built-in microphone on the

00:05:14.400 --> 00:05:16.370
Famicom's second player controller,

00:05:16.370 --> 00:05:18.820
there are many things in this 
world that make no sense.

00:05:18.820 --> 00:05:21.940
However, humans are meant 
to eat, poop, and sleep.

00:05:21.940 --> 00:05:24.410
Everything else we do is useless.

00:05:24.410 --> 00:05:27.630
Our creations fall into that category.

00:05:27.630 --> 00:05:29.300
So after making a pompous speech,

00:05:29.300 --> 00:05:31.400
all you're saying is that we make junk!

00:05:31.820 --> 00:05:33.270
Okay.

00:05:33.270 --> 00:05:38.120
So you do useless work 
making useless stuff?

00:05:38.120 --> 00:05:40.580
It seems that you didn't 
understand what I was saying.

00:05:40.580 --> 00:05:43.700
My point was that useless can 
be valuable in its own way.

00:05:43.700 --> 00:05:44.990
Yeah, but...

00:05:44.990 --> 00:05:47.150
If all Odd Jobs does 
is make useless stuff,

00:05:47.150 --> 00:05:51.140
doesn't that mean the 
members are also useless?

00:05:51.140 --> 00:05:51.960
What's with this kid?

00:05:52.320 --> 00:05:53.960
That's not nice, Daigoro-kun.

00:05:53.960 --> 00:05:57.420
Satsuki-chan, we can call off the tour.

00:05:57.420 --> 00:05:59.260
It's clear that these Odd Jobs people

00:05:59.260 --> 00:06:01.560
do useless work that 
doesn't help society.

00:06:01.560 --> 00:06:02.550
Wait a moment!

00:06:02.550 --> 00:06:05.350
While the Patriot may look 
useless, it is, in fact,

00:06:05.350 --> 00:06:06.820
a multimedia product which can be

00:06:06.820 --> 00:06:08.640
used in a number of useless games.

00:06:08.640 --> 00:06:10.310
Oh? Really?

00:06:10.310 --> 00:06:12.030
What kind of games are 
you talking about?

00:06:12.030 --> 00:06:13.080
For example...

00:06:13.250 --> 00:06:15.060
You can use the Patriot missile to whack

00:06:15.060 --> 00:06:16.730
the head of someone who pisses you off.

00:06:16.730 --> 00:06:18.650
You don't need the Patriot to do that!

00:06:19.940 --> 00:06:21.400
I knew it.

00:06:21.680 --> 00:06:23.920
I can't believe that people actually

00:06:23.920 --> 00:06:26.530
pay you scum to make this trash.

00:06:26.530 --> 00:06:27.330
Daigoro-kun?!

00:06:27.330 --> 00:06:29.540
You sound like a different person 
after the beating to your head!

00:06:30.110 --> 00:06:32.030
Satsuki, I'm going home.

00:06:32.030 --> 00:06:33.170
I've had enough.

00:06:33.170 --> 00:06:34.140
Daigoro-kun!

00:06:34.140 --> 00:06:35.220
Wait, boy.

00:06:35.220 --> 00:06:36.270
You didn't drink your Calcutta...

00:06:36.270 --> 00:06:37.960
Sorry, Mr. President.

00:06:37.960 --> 00:06:41.060
I don't like Calcutta or Meso Gear.

00:06:41.060 --> 00:06:42.090
I go for Bourbon.

00:06:42.090 --> 00:06:43.400
That's pretty hard-boiled!

00:06:43.400 --> 00:06:44.620
What's with this kid?!

00:06:44.620 --> 00:06:46.680
I'll need to work hard to find

00:06:46.680 --> 00:06:49.020
a real job so I don't 
end up like you slobs.

00:06:49.020 --> 00:06:50.730
Thanks for showing me what it's like

00:06:50.730 --> 00:06:53.230
at the bottom of society, Odd Jobs.

00:06:56.440 --> 00:06:58.860
Cheer up, Gin-san.

00:06:59.220 --> 00:07:01.200
A child wouldn't be able to understand

00:07:01.200 --> 00:07:02.900
how incredible Odd Jobs truly is.

00:07:02.900 --> 00:07:05.650
The other kids said they had fun.

00:07:05.650 --> 00:07:09.120
Though they tossed the Patriots 
we gave them as souvenirs.

00:07:09.560 --> 00:07:13.480
I started this business from scratch,

00:07:13.480 --> 00:07:15.850
and I kind of like it.

00:07:16.120 --> 00:07:17.660
But I guess kids aren't impressed...

00:07:17.660 --> 00:07:19.630
Th-That's not true!

00:07:19.840 --> 00:07:21.630
Okay, tell me this then.

00:07:22.080 --> 00:07:23.630
What can this be used for?

00:07:25.630 --> 00:07:27.000
Can't think of anything, right?!

00:07:27.000 --> 00:07:27.970
'Course you can't!

00:07:27.970 --> 00:07:29.410
I can't either!

00:07:29.410 --> 00:07:31.100
I'm no different from 
this piece of junk!

00:07:31.100 --> 00:07:32.530
Odd Jobs is trash!

00:07:32.530 --> 00:07:36.650
We do work that doesn't mean 
a damn thing to society!

00:07:37.720 --> 00:07:39.870
He's completely snapped.

00:07:39.870 --> 00:07:41.690
It must have been a big shock to him.

00:07:42.860 --> 00:07:44.650
Huh? Isn't that Hijikata-san?

00:07:44.900 --> 00:07:47.140
We patrol the streets to 
make sure there aren't any

00:07:47.140 --> 00:07:48.660
bad people doing bad things.

00:07:48.660 --> 00:07:51.430
That's the most essential 
job of a policeman.

00:07:51.430 --> 00:07:52.410
Ooh!

00:07:52.410 --> 00:07:53.670
What is it?

00:07:53.670 --> 00:07:55.910
Who would be a bad person?

00:07:56.510 --> 00:07:59.360
Anyone who breaks the law.

00:07:59.360 --> 00:08:02.210
So the law is always good?

00:08:02.210 --> 00:08:04.420
In most cases, the law 
can be considered good...

00:08:04.420 --> 00:08:05.850
I have a question then!

00:08:05.850 --> 00:08:08.580
You aren't allowed to drop down from 
a train platform to the tracks,

00:08:08.580 --> 00:08:10.070
but what if someone jumps down

00:08:10.070 --> 00:08:12.310
to save a drunk who 
happened to fall down?!

00:08:12.310 --> 00:08:13.560
Would someone who stays on the platform

00:08:13.560 --> 00:08:15.200
as the drunk dies be considered good?!

00:08:15.200 --> 00:08:17.770
You take those situations case by case.

00:08:17.770 --> 00:08:22.020
A law that's always changing 
can't be considered a proper law!

00:08:22.410 --> 00:08:24.400
I didn't word that right.

00:08:24.400 --> 00:08:27.400
A person who makes trouble 
for others is a bad person.

00:08:27.400 --> 00:08:28.870
The law doesn't matter.

00:08:28.870 --> 00:08:29.950
He just threw out the law!

00:08:29.950 --> 00:08:31.670
He got sick of trying 
and threw out the law!

00:08:31.670 --> 00:08:34.990
By that logic, you would 
be a criminal for exposing

00:08:34.990 --> 00:08:36.160
us to second-hand smoke!

00:08:36.270 --> 00:08:38.620
I'm sorry! Too much smoke for you?!

00:08:38.620 --> 00:08:40.350
Please forgive me! Please forgive me!

00:08:40.350 --> 00:08:41.130
This is bad!

00:08:41.130 --> 00:08:42.050
He's about to lose it!

00:08:42.050 --> 00:08:43.170
He's about to turn into a criminal!

00:08:43.170 --> 00:08:45.390
Could you explain how much 
trouble a person must cause

00:08:45.390 --> 00:08:47.250
to be considered a criminal?

00:08:47.250 --> 00:08:48.090
For example...

00:08:48.660 --> 00:08:50.980
We have an individual getting 
the snot knocked out of him

00:08:50.980 --> 00:08:52.250
by the woman he keeps stalking.

00:08:52.250 --> 00:08:53.970
Which one is the criminal?

00:08:55.920 --> 00:08:56.980
Uh...

00:08:56.980 --> 00:08:58.860
I was just joking.

00:08:58.860 --> 00:09:00.600
In reality, policemen are...

00:09:01.340 --> 00:09:04.810
...people involved in the production 
and sale of this Patriot.

00:09:04.810 --> 00:09:06.970
He threw out everything and 
became a Patriot salesman!

00:09:06.970 --> 00:09:07.640
What's going on?!

00:09:07.640 --> 00:09:08.400
Is this a new fad?!

00:09:08.400 --> 00:09:09.500
Pathetic.

00:09:09.500 --> 00:09:11.510
You switch jobs when 
the going gets tough?

00:09:11.510 --> 00:09:13.310
Guess they weren't lying 
when they said the police

00:09:13.310 --> 00:09:14.540
in Japan were going to hell.

00:09:16.270 --> 00:09:18.090
Now it's Hijikata-san's turn to lose it.

00:09:18.090 --> 00:09:20.330
I didn't realize you could 
use the Patriot that way.

00:09:20.330 --> 00:09:21.540
Stop this foolishness.

00:09:22.150 --> 00:09:23.420
Tsukuyo-san?

00:09:23.720 --> 00:09:25.190
Please, lady!

00:09:25.190 --> 00:09:26.970
We want to learn more about

00:09:26.970 --> 00:09:28.670
the people who work in Yoshiwara!

00:09:28.890 --> 00:09:31.430
And I told you to come 
back in a hundred years.

00:09:31.430 --> 00:09:32.430
Ooh!

00:09:32.950 --> 00:09:35.790
Could you at least teach us how to

00:09:35.790 --> 00:09:38.060
whip a man in a way 
that brings pleasure?

00:09:38.060 --> 00:09:41.060
There's a very familiar 
freak mixed in there!

00:09:41.380 --> 00:09:44.930
Now, that's the last 
thing I would teach you.

00:09:44.930 --> 00:09:46.930
I'm in a relationship 
with this guy right now.

00:09:46.930 --> 00:09:48.350
So you'll take responsibility

00:09:48.350 --> 00:09:50.440
if something goes wrong 
when the time comes?

00:09:50.440 --> 00:09:51.470
Nothing will go wrong!

00:09:51.470 --> 00:09:53.070
It's all in your head!

00:09:53.350 --> 00:09:56.740
I guess it'll be too late
if something goes wrong.

00:09:56.740 --> 00:09:58.410
Well, it's probably a good idea

00:09:58.410 --> 00:10:00.660
to learn the general basics now.

00:10:00.780 --> 00:10:02.100
Allow me to explain then.

00:10:02.100 --> 00:10:04.490
If this is that, and this 
is where you do that...

00:10:04.490 --> 00:10:06.920
What are you doing with that Patriot?!

00:10:08.220 --> 00:10:10.420
That's what girls are like?!

00:10:11.680 --> 00:10:14.220
I was trying to give them a simple 
explanation without revealing anything...

00:10:14.220 --> 00:10:15.910
Stop playing dumb!

00:10:15.910 --> 00:10:17.880
Teach me the secret 
techniques of Yoshiwara!

00:10:17.880 --> 00:10:20.200
Well, as you can see, our job isn't

00:10:20.200 --> 00:10:21.940
always a walk in the park.

00:10:22.270 --> 00:10:24.280
However, we never give up.

00:10:24.280 --> 00:10:25.940
Believe in a better tomorrow 
and stay on the trail.

00:10:26.190 --> 00:10:27.760
That's how you become a stalker.

00:10:27.760 --> 00:10:28.940
That's not a job!

00:10:29.310 --> 00:10:29.990
Oh!

00:10:29.990 --> 00:10:31.280
Yes, what is it?

00:10:31.280 --> 00:10:33.830
Do you ever want to die?

00:10:33.830 --> 00:10:35.200
What kind of question is that?!

00:10:35.530 --> 00:10:36.780
A very good question.

00:10:36.770 --> 00:10:38.200
It's not a good question!

00:10:38.460 --> 00:10:42.220
A job is supposed to be painful.

00:10:42.220 --> 00:10:45.700
In that case, you should look 
for pain that you can enjoy.

00:10:45.700 --> 00:10:47.840
How can you say that while 
pretending to be a professional?!

00:10:47.940 --> 00:10:50.320
That is naive!

00:10:51.650 --> 00:10:55.410
There are many people with 
jobs they absolutely hate!

00:10:55.410 --> 00:10:58.550
Society needs these people to function!

00:10:58.550 --> 00:10:59.850
Look at me!

00:11:00.440 --> 00:11:03.530
You think I want to be a Patriot?!

00:11:03.530 --> 00:11:04.280
Hey!

00:11:04.280 --> 00:11:06.810
I seriously have no idea what 
a Patriot is supposed to be!

00:11:07.010 --> 00:11:08.710
But I don't have a choice!

00:11:08.710 --> 00:11:10.890
If I don't do this, who will?!

00:11:10.890 --> 00:11:13.240
This world needs Patriots!

00:11:13.240 --> 00:11:14.200
The hell it does!

00:11:14.670 --> 00:11:17.200
The people who always blame others...

00:11:17.200 --> 00:11:19.420
...can never have a better life.

00:11:19.420 --> 00:11:20.670
How would you...

00:11:20.670 --> 00:11:23.360
How would you know how it 
feels to be a Patriot?!

00:11:23.360 --> 00:11:24.310
I know.

00:11:24.310 --> 00:11:24.830
Huh?

00:11:25.330 --> 00:11:27.330
After all... After all...

00:11:28.340 --> 00:11:31.980
I'm working two jobs as 
both a Patriot and a stalker!

00:11:31.980 --> 00:11:34.090
That just means you fail at life!

00:11:36.250 --> 00:11:38.430
Y-You too?

00:11:38.720 --> 00:11:42.070
Yeah, you don't have to 
bear the burden alone.

00:11:42.070 --> 00:11:43.930
Ask me for help.

00:11:45.540 --> 00:11:47.600
Th-Thank you.

00:11:48.660 --> 00:11:50.940
Uh, excuse me.

00:11:51.150 --> 00:11:53.690
So what's a Patriot?

00:11:55.100 --> 00:11:56.200
No idea.

00:12:02.370 --> 00:12:04.870
What are you people doing?

00:12:04.870 --> 00:12:08.880
You grown-ups let a bunch 
of kids bully you around.

00:12:10.750 --> 00:12:14.700
It's the job of a grown-up to 
teach kids what's important.

00:12:15.350 --> 00:12:19.260
We can't let their tour end like this.

00:12:21.660 --> 00:12:24.020
Daigoro, there's a letter for you.

00:12:24.310 --> 00:12:25.580
Letter?

00:12:27.520 --> 00:12:32.070
<b>Invitation to an educational 
tour of a Patriot factory.</b>

00:12:29.130 --> 00:12:30.520
What's this?

00:12:32.780 --> 00:12:34.030
Daigoro!

00:12:34.740 --> 00:12:36.990
You received an invitation too?

00:12:36.990 --> 00:12:38.490
Oh, you guys also got one?

00:12:38.490 --> 00:12:42.490
<b>Invitation to an educational 
tour of a Patriot factory.</b>

00:12:38.870 --> 00:12:40.320
I was gonna ignore it,

00:12:40.320 --> 00:12:42.490
but I heard that we'll 
get Dokkiriman stickers.

00:12:42.820 --> 00:12:45.500
So, what's a Patriot factory?

00:12:45.500 --> 00:12:47.370
<b>Welcome to the Patriot Factory</b>

00:12:47.380 --> 00:12:50.250
We've been waiting for you, kids.

00:12:50.460 --> 00:12:53.090
You brats, I mean, nice children

00:12:53.090 --> 00:12:55.960
were chosen from around the world

00:12:55.960 --> 00:12:58.840
to tour this factory of dreams!

00:12:59.270 --> 00:13:00.440
I'm Pachi!

00:13:00.440 --> 00:13:01.810
I'm Gura!

00:13:01.810 --> 00:13:05.890
We'll be your guides on this 
tour of the factory of dreams!

00:13:07.890 --> 00:13:10.160
Isn't this a total rip-off of 
Charlie and the Chocolate Factory?

00:13:10.160 --> 00:13:14.150
Excuse me, what is the 
purpose of this tour?

00:13:14.280 --> 00:13:16.990
What? You don't appreciate 
our invitation?

00:13:16.990 --> 00:13:18.280
Feel free to leave.

00:13:18.280 --> 00:13:20.470
But you won't get any 
Dokkiriman stickers.

00:13:20.470 --> 00:13:23.660
And you'll lose your chance 
to learn what Patriots are.

00:13:23.930 --> 00:13:25.970
Who cares about Patriots...

00:13:26.700 --> 00:13:28.040
Look! Look!

00:13:28.040 --> 00:13:29.250
It's a Patriot factory!

00:13:29.250 --> 00:13:30.670
No way! I don't believe it!

00:13:30.670 --> 00:13:33.170
I never imagined that a Patriot 
factory would be here!

00:13:33.550 --> 00:13:36.050
I heard that they were only produced by

00:13:36.050 --> 00:13:38.310
NASA, the FBI, and the NBA!

00:13:38.560 --> 00:13:40.510
Let's take a look.

00:13:40.510 --> 00:13:41.720
Wait, Sarutobi!

00:13:46.970 --> 00:13:49.280
Chief, I found some suspicious people

00:13:49.280 --> 00:13:50.980
who were investigating the Patriot.

00:13:50.980 --> 00:13:52.350
I immediately shot them down.

00:13:52.630 --> 00:13:53.550
Roger that.

00:13:53.550 --> 00:13:56.120
So the Succeed Committee 
has finally made its move.

00:13:56.120 --> 00:13:57.730
The time of Ragnarok is upon us.

00:13:57.730 --> 00:13:59.320
We must hasten the 
development of the Patriot.

00:13:59.500 --> 00:14:01.560
I also see some funny-looking kids.

00:14:01.560 --> 00:14:02.740
Should I take them out?

00:14:05.480 --> 00:14:07.330
They are my guests.

00:14:08.560 --> 00:14:10.410
The last hope of humanity.

00:14:10.410 --> 00:14:12.580
The children who will 
inherit the Patriots.

00:14:12.810 --> 00:14:15.670
Welcome to the Patriot factory tour.

00:14:15.850 --> 00:14:17.130
Chief!

00:14:17.130 --> 00:14:19.340
The kids aren't interested 
in the Patriot.

00:14:19.790 --> 00:14:20.770
I see.

00:14:20.770 --> 00:14:23.350
But you've seen too much already.

00:14:23.790 --> 00:14:25.220
Take them out...

00:14:26.290 --> 00:14:27.900
You can leave.

00:14:27.900 --> 00:14:29.750
Be careful on the way home.

00:14:31.230 --> 00:14:32.590
This way.

00:14:32.590 --> 00:14:34.840
Seriously! We should leave!

00:14:34.820 --> 00:14:37.230
They'll kill us if we leave!

00:14:37.590 --> 00:14:41.730
We'll have to do as they say and 
tour the Patriot factory.

00:14:41.730 --> 00:14:42.990
But...

00:14:42.990 --> 00:14:45.080
Take a look at this.

00:14:42.990 --> 00:14:48.490
<b>History of the Patriot</b>

00:14:45.080 --> 00:14:46.850
You can see the history and

00:14:46.850 --> 00:14:48.490
development of the Patriot here.

00:14:48.990 --> 00:14:52.380
Here, you will find the 
current Patriot design.

00:14:52.380 --> 00:14:55.530
However, Patriots have been 
around since the Jomon period.

00:14:55.530 --> 00:14:56.630
Thanks to trial and error,

00:14:56.630 --> 00:14:58.700
we were able to create one of 
the essential tools in our life.

00:14:58.700 --> 00:15:00.260
I've never used one before.

00:15:00.510 --> 00:15:01.880
This would be the father of the Patriot,

00:15:01.880 --> 00:15:04.150
the oldest one known, 
which was created by

00:15:04.150 --> 00:15:05.730
the chief of the Zugomanda tribe.

00:15:05.730 --> 00:15:07.010
Isn't that a drumstick?

00:15:07.210 --> 00:15:10.860
It may look like one, but 
this is, in fact, a Patriot.

00:15:10.860 --> 00:15:11.880
Look over here.

00:15:11.880 --> 00:15:13.440
It says "not for 
consumption" on the side.

00:15:13.440 --> 00:15:15.270
It has to be edible if 
there are preservatives!

00:15:15.410 --> 00:15:19.190
The original Patriot was known as the

00:15:19.190 --> 00:15:21.670
boned Patriot or Kin(Patriot)Man.

00:15:21.670 --> 00:15:23.360
There's only one word 
that would fit in there!

00:15:23.710 --> 00:15:25.030
In the Heian period,

00:15:25.030 --> 00:15:27.400
the Tang ambassador Zugomaru Kakinomoto

00:15:27.400 --> 00:15:28.620
altered the design significantly.

00:15:29.350 --> 00:15:31.520
He brought ingredients 
back from the Tang

00:15:31.520 --> 00:15:32.850
to make it a Spicy Patriot...

00:15:32.850 --> 00:15:34.240
That's just spicy chicken!

00:15:34.240 --> 00:15:35.910
And somebody took a bite out of it!

00:15:35.910 --> 00:15:38.140
Zugomaru's still got 
some around his mouth!

00:15:38.140 --> 00:15:39.290
And in the Sengoku period,

00:15:39.290 --> 00:15:42.300
Zugomanzo turned the 
Patriot into something.

00:15:42.300 --> 00:15:44.170
Why is it part of a combo now?!

00:15:44.170 --> 00:15:45.740
Did Zugomanzo even do anything?!

00:15:45.740 --> 00:15:47.990
This is like the history 
of fried chicken!

00:15:47.990 --> 00:15:51.310
And eventually we reached 
the current Patriot design.

00:15:51.310 --> 00:15:52.250
Why?!

00:15:52.250 --> 00:15:54.640
You skipped over the 
most important part!

00:15:54.850 --> 00:15:56.900
Now that you have some basic 
knowledge of the Patriot,

00:15:56.900 --> 00:15:58.940
we'll give you a tour of the factory.

00:15:59.740 --> 00:16:02.110
We'll see how the 
Patriot is constructed.

00:16:03.070 --> 00:16:07.640
As you can see, the Patriot 
is made up of three parts.

00:16:08.360 --> 00:16:10.430
The tissue box, which 
is known as the solid.

00:16:10.430 --> 00:16:13.620
Uh, you called it a tissue 
box, so why call it the solid?

00:16:13.620 --> 00:16:16.620
The toilet paper, which 
is known as the naked.

00:16:16.620 --> 00:16:19.020
And the stick.

00:16:19.020 --> 00:16:20.170
Why did you stop coming up with names?!

00:16:20.540 --> 00:16:24.420
You jack in the three 
parts to create a Patriot.

00:16:25.130 --> 00:16:27.700
Look at the conveyor belt.

00:16:27.930 --> 00:16:29.880
I don't see a thing.

00:16:29.890 --> 00:16:32.310
Maybe the place is a mess 
because the chief is dead?

00:16:34.310 --> 00:16:36.940
The chief is moving down the belt!

00:16:37.140 --> 00:16:40.830
The first step is to fix 
the broken factory chief.

00:16:40.830 --> 00:16:41.600
That's where you start?!

00:16:41.600 --> 00:16:44.230
Broken chief?! You're 
the ones who broke him!

00:16:44.230 --> 00:16:45.910
The factory chief was 
broken to begin with.

00:16:45.910 --> 00:16:48.320
Nobody respects the chief!

00:16:48.530 --> 00:16:51.180
First, we use tissues 
to wipe up the bloody body.

00:16:51.180 --> 00:16:52.970
That's one of the 
parts for the Patriot!

00:16:52.970 --> 00:16:55.010
Start assembling the Patriot already!

00:16:55.010 --> 00:16:58.130
Next, we use toilet paper to 
wipe away his bloody past.

00:16:58.130 --> 00:16:59.680
Who cares about his past?!

00:16:59.680 --> 00:17:01.620
Make the Patriot already!

00:17:01.810 --> 00:17:04.490
And then you use the 
Patriot to wake him up.

00:17:04.490 --> 00:17:06.380
The Patriot's already finished!

00:17:06.380 --> 00:17:08.220
Why would you use a Patriot 
to make a Patriot?

00:17:08.480 --> 00:17:10.200
Then you repeat the process three times.

00:17:10.200 --> 00:17:12.340
You're just abusing him!

00:17:12.340 --> 00:17:15.510
And aren't these the 
people who were shot?

00:17:15.510 --> 00:17:18.190
The chief must settle past accounts 
before he can be revived.

00:17:18.190 --> 00:17:19.730
They're just getting revenge!

00:17:19.730 --> 00:17:23.230
<b>Heal</b>

00:17:20.130 --> 00:17:23.230
And finally, we send the factory 
chief into the healing machine.

00:17:24.820 --> 00:17:26.230
The factory chief is complete!

00:17:26.230 --> 00:17:28.240
Nothing changed!

00:17:28.240 --> 00:17:30.660
This is the completed form 
of the factory chief.

00:17:30.660 --> 00:17:32.630
He was born broken.

00:17:32.630 --> 00:17:34.740
What was the point of 
that whole process then?!

00:17:34.740 --> 00:17:35.940
In the second step,

00:17:35.940 --> 00:17:38.110
we give the assembled 
factory chief motivation.

00:17:38.110 --> 00:17:39.390
Otherwise known as giving 
the factory chief a goal.

00:17:39.390 --> 00:17:41.130
Enough with the chief!

00:17:41.350 --> 00:17:42.760
The chief is absolutely necessary

00:17:42.760 --> 00:17:45.080
for the production of a Patriot,

00:17:45.080 --> 00:17:45.840
so this can't be avoided.

00:17:45.840 --> 00:17:47.820
When are you going to make a Patriot?!

00:17:47.820 --> 00:17:50.100
This is turning into a factory 
for making factory chiefs!

00:17:49.380 --> 00:17:51.090
<b>I could only see the stars back then.</b>

00:17:50.090 --> 00:17:51.090
Hm? What's that?

00:17:51.400 --> 00:17:53.800
They put him in a school uniform.

00:17:56.350 --> 00:17:58.060
It's so fast!

00:17:58.060 --> 00:17:59.610
I can barely keep up!

00:17:59.600 --> 00:18:01.020
Hey! Look over there!

00:18:01.020 --> 00:18:06.480
<b>Do your best! Become the best 
factory chief in Japan!!</b>

00:18:01.350 --> 00:18:04.190
Hooray! Hooray! Do your best!

00:18:04.190 --> 00:18:06.480
Why are they acting like 
he's on a train to Tokyo?!

00:18:06.700 --> 00:18:08.480
We believe in you!

00:18:08.490 --> 00:18:10.740
You can become the best 
factory chief in Japan!

00:18:10.750 --> 00:18:12.660
You can do it, Facto!

00:18:12.660 --> 00:18:14.050
His name is Facto?!

00:18:14.320 --> 00:18:15.240
Hey!

00:18:15.240 --> 00:18:17.420
What kind of process is this?!

00:18:17.420 --> 00:18:19.570
Now we have some kind of funky set!

00:18:20.460 --> 00:18:22.460
You want to become a factory chief?!

00:18:22.460 --> 00:18:24.090
You were destined to inherit

00:18:24.090 --> 00:18:25.910
my toilet paper business from the

00:18:25.910 --> 00:18:27.760
day you were born!

00:18:28.080 --> 00:18:29.240
Who's that?!

00:18:29.240 --> 00:18:31.480
Go to Edo to work for a tissue factory?!

00:18:31.480 --> 00:18:32.610
Don't look down on me!

00:18:32.610 --> 00:18:35.970
You think that toilet paper's 
only meant for wiping the ass?!

00:18:36.380 --> 00:18:39.270
Why is the factory chief's father here?!

00:18:39.270 --> 00:18:41.580
This must be a flashback.

00:18:41.580 --> 00:18:42.980
He was kicked out of his home,

00:18:42.980 --> 00:18:44.610
which would explain the previous scene.

00:18:44.770 --> 00:18:46.020
Darling!

00:18:46.020 --> 00:18:47.450
Stop it!

00:18:47.450 --> 00:18:51.640
Our son is making paper in his own way!

00:18:51.640 --> 00:18:52.740
Now his mother's here?!

00:18:52.740 --> 00:18:53.960
Let me go, Isako!

00:18:53.960 --> 00:18:55.420
This is a discussion between men!

00:18:55.420 --> 00:18:56.620
Ah, Facto!

00:18:56.620 --> 00:19:00.080
Where are you going?!
 I'm not finished with you yet!

00:18:59.750 --> 00:19:01.330
<b>Roof</b>

00:19:00.100 --> 00:19:01.960
What are they trying to do?!

00:19:01.960 --> 00:19:03.330
Oh, he's wearing his old clothes again.

00:19:04.390 --> 00:19:05.970
Oh, chief.

00:19:05.970 --> 00:19:07.090
Good work.

00:19:07.090 --> 00:19:08.500
He has a buddy with him now!

00:19:08.680 --> 00:19:11.350
Why are you taking a nap here?

00:19:11.350 --> 00:19:12.320
He's not taking a nap!

00:19:12.320 --> 00:19:14.510
He's been out cold on the 
conveyor belt this whole time!

00:19:16.060 --> 00:19:19.520
Thinking about old times again?

00:19:20.260 --> 00:19:22.540
Your old man was really something.

00:19:22.540 --> 00:19:27.520
A family of toilet paper men 
who refused to use tissues.

00:19:27.760 --> 00:19:29.660
When wiping his ass,

00:19:29.660 --> 00:19:32.130
blowing his nose, writing down notes...

00:19:32.130 --> 00:19:34.750
He even used toilet paper 
for the tires on his car.

00:19:34.750 --> 00:19:36.530
Is the last one even necessary?!

00:19:36.960 --> 00:19:39.390
You left your home 
because you didn't want

00:19:39.390 --> 00:19:40.910
to follow in his footsteps.

00:19:41.240 --> 00:19:43.810
And so, you became the 
chief of a tissue factory.

00:19:44.690 --> 00:19:47.690
You still refuse to use toilet paper?

00:19:49.350 --> 00:19:51.810
You're just as stubborn as your father.

00:19:51.810 --> 00:19:53.390
Still, chief...

00:19:53.390 --> 00:19:56.360
If your old man saw you now,

00:19:56.360 --> 00:19:59.390
I'm sure he'd be willing to use tissues.

00:20:03.990 --> 00:20:06.930
He never changed...

00:20:06.930 --> 00:20:10.700
He was always so stubborn.

00:20:10.990 --> 00:20:13.820
He used toilet paper to wipe 
his ass and blow his nose.

00:20:14.550 --> 00:20:16.920
When your tissues first went on sale,

00:20:16.920 --> 00:20:18.820
he used toilet paper 
to wipe away the tears.

00:20:19.900 --> 00:20:22.700
Tissues weren't good enough for him.

00:20:23.060 --> 00:20:24.340
Chief!

00:20:24.340 --> 00:20:26.140
What are you thinking?!

00:20:26.140 --> 00:20:28.360
You really think this 
product will sell?!

00:20:28.360 --> 00:20:29.710
I can't go along with this!

00:20:29.710 --> 00:20:31.030
Hey, did you hear?

00:20:31.030 --> 00:20:35.220
The chief has come up 
with a crazy new product.

00:20:35.380 --> 00:20:37.120
D-Don't tell me...

00:20:37.120 --> 00:20:38.910
His job's on the line.

00:20:38.910 --> 00:20:41.520
But he insists on going 
through with the idea.

00:20:41.520 --> 00:20:42.220
It can't be...

00:20:42.400 --> 00:20:44.730
Hey, what kind of product 
are we talking about?

00:20:45.250 --> 00:20:46.190
No way...

00:20:46.730 --> 00:20:49.890
Toilet paper and tissue join together.

00:20:49.890 --> 00:20:53.480
The ultimate paper for 
wiping away your tears.

00:20:54.560 --> 00:20:58.150
Th-That's the Patriot!

00:21:00.230 --> 00:21:04.750
We will now proceed to the final 
step for creating a Patriot.

00:21:05.450 --> 00:21:08.330
Look! Above the conveyor belt!

00:21:08.750 --> 00:21:11.750
Come, Patriot factory chief!

00:21:15.880 --> 00:21:19.470
Do you still think that 
Patriots are trash?

00:21:19.860 --> 00:21:23.510
Do you still think that 
this job is trash?

00:21:23.510 --> 00:21:25.660
Jobs aren't meant to be compared.

00:21:25.660 --> 00:21:28.770
When you willingly work for 
the sake of someone else,

00:21:28.770 --> 00:21:30.020
you're doing your job.

00:21:30.440 --> 00:21:33.440
Every job deserves respect.

00:21:33.440 --> 00:21:37.530
Because the world needs 
all of us to do our jobs.

00:21:38.960 --> 00:21:41.620
Would you like to try doing your job?

00:21:43.370 --> 00:21:47.170
Go help the factory chief.

00:21:48.410 --> 00:21:50.500
K-Kids...

00:21:51.220 --> 00:21:55.500
You should have just gotten 
your ass off the conveyor belt!

00:21:57.230 --> 00:21:58.830
Good work, everyone.

00:21:58.830 --> 00:22:01.010
Yeah, we took out the trash.

00:22:01.180 --> 00:22:04.490
Those damn fools wasted our 
time with that stupid show.

00:22:06.500 --> 00:22:08.680
That was an educational experience.

00:22:08.680 --> 00:22:09.610
Yep.

00:23:40.070 --> 00:23:44.990
<b>Next Episode: What Happens 
Twice Can Happen Thrice</b>

00:23:41.020 --> 00:23:42.060
Next time:

00:23:42.060 --> 00:23:44.380
What happens twice can happen thrice!
